meta {
  name: Presign Rewrite Document
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/policies/{{soldPolicyId}}/rewrite/presign
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "new_business_application",
    "filename": "rewrite-application.pdf",
    "contentType": "application/pdf",
    "size": 2048
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.getStatus() === 201) {
    const body = res.getBody();
    bru.setVar("rewriteDocumentKey", body.key);
    bru.setVar("rewriteDocumentUploadUrl", body.uploadUrl);
  }
}

tests {
  test("returns 201 Created", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(201);
  });

  test("signs the key under the rewrite prefix", function () {
    // Its own namespace, not the lead one — see the docs.
    const key = res.getBody().key;
    expect(key).to.contain("agencies/");
    expect(key).to.contain("policy-rewrites/");
    expect(key).to.contain("/nba/");
  });

  test("does not sign under the sold-deals prefix", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().key).to.not.contain("sold-deals/");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /policies/:id/rewrite/presign — a document on an in-progress rewrite

  Module `deal_audits`, permission **`deal_audits:write`** — the same gate as the
  rewrite itself: whoever may book one may upload its paperwork. Data scope is
  enforced by `loadOwnedPolicy` before anything is signed, so a presign cannot
  probe for policies outside the caller's scope.

  ## Why it exists

  The wizard uploads while it is still being filled in, so there is no deal yet
  to scope a document to — it is anchored on whatever the flow *does* have. A
  sale has a lead (`POST /sold-deals/documents/presign`); a transfer has a ticket
  (`POST /crm/service-tickets/:id/policy-transfer/presign`); a **rewrite has the
  policy being replaced**, and the household is read off it server-side so a
  caller cannot name one it does not own.

  Without this endpoint the rewrite had nothing to upload against. The web wizard
  fell through to the lead presign with an empty `leadId`, every upload 400'd,
  and because the New Business Application is **required** the whole flow could
  not be submitted.

  ## The key prefix is the ownership check

  Keys come back under `agencies/<agencyId>/policy-rewrites/<householdId>/…`,
  with `/nba/` appended for the application kind.

  ⚠ **Its own namespace, disjoint from the others.** The first cut of PAC-126
  verified rewrite attachments with the *lead* purpose
  (`sold-deals/<householdId>`), mixing two different id spaces under one prefix —
  so a key minted against household `X` would have replayed against lead `X` and
  passed `assertKeyOwnership`. It is disjoint from the transfer's
  `policy-transfers/<householdId>` too, for the smaller version of the same
  reason: the two flows are gated on different permissions
  (`deal_audits:write` against `crm_service:write`), so a key minted by one
  should not be presentable to the other.

  ## Body

  | Field | Type | Req | Notes |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | `kind` | `discount_proof` \| `new_business_application` | no | Defaults to `discount_proof`. Decides both the accepted content types and the key prefix. |
  | `filename` | string(1–255) | yes | Sanitized into the key; `..` is unrepresentable. |
  | `contentType` | enum | yes | PDF/JPEG/PNG for a discount proof, **PDF only** for the application. |
  | `size` | int | yes | ≤ 10 MB. A claim, not evidence — `POST :id/rewrite` re-derives the real size with `HeadObject`. |

  No anchor in the body: the policy is the path parameter.

  ## Response `201`

  ```json
  {
    "key": "agencies/665f…/policy-rewrites/665f…/nba/2026/9f2c-rewrite-application.pdf",
    "uploadUrl": "http://localhost:9000/sfa-uploads/…?X-Amz-Signature=…",
    "requiredHeaders": { "Content-Type": "application/pdf" },
    "expiresIn": 900
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | Code | When |
  |---|---|
  | `400` | The policy has no household; a non-PDF `contentType` for the application kind; a declared size over 10 MB. |
  | `403` | Caller lacks `deal_audits:write`, or the module is disabled for the agency. |
  | `404` | No such policy, or it is outside the caller's data scope. |

  ## Run order

  Needs `soldPolicyId`. Feeds `Upload Rewrite Document` (seq 4), whose key
  `Rewrite Policy` (seq 5) then declares.
}
